            <div xml:id="d54-a26">

                <pb facs="0171" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg153"/>

                <head>[Extract from deposition of William Brennan, sealer (sailing master, boat
                    steerer).]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">pelagic sealing.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The cow is 3 years old before she bears young. The pups are about 45 days old
                    before they can go into the water, but they nurse the mother as long as they
                    stay on the island. They are called “black” and “gray” pups—black before they
                    shed their first coat and gray afterwards. As they grow older the gray turns
                    darker, except upon the neck and head, but the color of the hair does not affect
                    the fur, which can be seen by parting it.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Brennan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>]</seg>
                    <signed rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. A.
                            McKenzie</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Notary
                    Public.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
